Z||000006||rockcrawl||02-04-2001||09:15 PM||||If you have a lot of patience, it can be done. I did the one for my Countach replica. I used the old pieces as patterns on some black leather. I used two different grades of leather, the top half was smooth and tight and the bottom was soft and had a gathered look. I must have spent 3 or 4 days stitching it by hand. I'd just sit down in front of the TV and stitch until my fingers were sore. The results were very good but I probably wouldn't do it again.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/int2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/int2.jpg</A> <BR>I don't know why my fortunecity links don't work here. If you want to see the picture, copy and paste the addy into your browser.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 02-04-2001).]||||reg||1
